A||N||9||pollock||Gran Prix wheels:  do they fit||||3
Z||000000||pollock||10-18-1999||11:05 AM||||I'm planning on 16" wheels for my next go-round on tires, and i really like some of the wheels i've seen on new Gran Prixs.  <P>I know that they're mostly 16s, and five lug, with about the right offset, but i'm wondering if the bolt pattern is the same, and exactly what the width and offset are.<P>Maybe one of you has a Gran Prix and could help out.  Please specify what year and what wheels you have.||||reg||3
Z||000001||David||10-18-1999||12:48 PM||||I think that the GP's have a different bolt circle.  Check out: <A HREF="http://www.tswnet.com/tables/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tswnet.com/tables/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||10-18-1999||01:02 PM||||Fiero's are 5 x 100mm. GP's are 5 x 115mm bolt spacing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||10-18-1999||09:06 PM||||What about the late model Sunfire GT 3 spoke alloy wheels? I think they would look good and they already have the Pontiac logo on them.||||reg||5
Z||000004||terryk||10-18-1999||09:36 PM||||They should be 5 x 100mm. Yes, they would fit.<P>5 X 115mm is reserved for the JAx HD brakes on the X and A cars and C/H cars it's standard. Don't know about N cars. They might have a HD brake option available.<P>Too bad the Fiero never had a real 10.25" HD brake option.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 10-19-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||pollock||10-19-1999||03:09 PM||||Cooter, how dare you suggest 3 spoke wheels?  Just kidding.<P>Terry, can you give me a rundown on what the X,C,H,A,and N cars are?||||reg||2
Z||000006||Cooter||10-19-1999||08:25 PM||||Pollock,<BR>I have a friend that had a Sunfire GT, the only cool thing about that car was the wheels! It was really a dog.||||reg||1
Z||000007||terryk||10-19-1999||11:24 PM||||X is Citation/Phoenix/Omega, et al.<BR>A is Celebrity/Ciera/6000/Century, et al.<BR>C/H is Bonneville/Park Ave/Eighty-Eight, et al.<BR>N is Calais/Grand Am/Skylark, et al.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||lowCG||10-20-1999||12:54 AM||||Some other cars that use the 5X100 bolt pattern are Toyota(Celica,Camry),Subaru,Chrysler FWD,Mazda(323,MX3),Volkswagen(VR6 cars,Passat).<BR>Don't know anything about any difference in hub diameters,would need to check that before any purchase for sure.||||reg||1
Z||000009||deceler8||10-20-1999||12:38 PM||||Ran across this page on Fiero Secrets...<BR> <A HREF="http://members.xoom.com/fierov6/OSG/wheels.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.xoom.com/fierov6/OSG/wheels.html</A> <P>A pretty complete listing of what will fit...was surprised to see that Dodge Shadow wheels will fit the Fiero...just sold my Shadow after buying the Fiero...had I known, I would have kept the wheels.<P>Now all I would like to know is what wings will fit the Fiero, rather than get scalped for a genuine Fiero wing...||||reg||1
